      <ul class="faq-list" id="faq-list">
        <li class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-q">
            What is Coreweaver Labs VaaS?
            <span class="faq-caret" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <p class="faq-a">Coreweaver Labs VaaS (Verification-as-a-Service) is an AI-native compliance infrastructure layer that enables CSRD-regulated enterprises to generate, audit, and publish immutable verification records for ESG disclosures. It is built on the ARM Framework and is developed by Coreweaver Labs, Inc., founded by Mason Nguyen.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-q">
            How does VaaS satisfy CSRD's assurance requirements?
            <span class="faq-caret" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <p class="faq-a">CSRD requires limited assurance (Phase 1) moving to reasonable assurance (Phase 2) on sustainability disclosures. VaaS produces an Immutable Audit Log — a cryptographically traceable record of every verification step — that assurance providers can independently inspect, dramatically reducing the effort and cost of third-party assurance engagements.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-q">
            Which CSRD standards does VaaS cover?
            <span class="faq-caret" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <p class="faq-a">VaaS is initially scoped to the cross-cutting ESRS standards (ESRS 1, ESRS 2) and the environmental standards (ESRS E1 through E5), with governance and social standards on the roadmap. The Mandate Chain primitive is designed to extend to any disclosure framework including GRI, TCFD, and ISSB.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-q">
            What is the ARM Framework?
            <span class="faq-caret" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <p class="faq-a">The ARM Framework (Autonomous Resource Management) is the shared AI infrastructure developed by Coreweaver Labs. Its five primitives — Mandate Chain, Signal Architecture, Durable State, Graceful Escalation, and Immutable Audit Log — provide the coordination and traceability layer that powers VaaS. The ARM Framework is also deployed across the Arctura Network and ARM infrastructure nodes.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-q">
            Who needs VaaS, and when?
            <span class="faq-caret" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <p class="faq-a">VaaS is designed for large enterprises subject to the EU Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive — including companies with 250+ employees, €40M+ revenue, or €20M+ balance sheet operating in the EU. Phase 1 reporting (for companies already subject to NFRD) began for FY2024. Phase 2 (large non-listed EU companies) begins FY2025. Non-EU companies with significant EU operations face CSRD from FY2028.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-q">
            How does VaaS integrate with existing systems?
            <span class="faq-caret" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <p class="faq-a">VaaS connects to enterprise data sources via the Signal Architecture layer — supporting API, SFTP, and direct database connections to ERP systems (SAP, Oracle), GHG accounting platforms (Persefoni, Watershed), supplier portals, and custom data warehouses. No rip-and-replace required.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
